From 2d5efca5b1612d8836afbd8acbb81076496c42e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: airidosas252 <airidaslideikis@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:30:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/20] tu: Fix memory growth, XFB and mesh keys with
 barycentric libraries

 - Retained post-link NIR used to be kept as live nir_shader objects in
   the never-evicting device cache, about 250 KiB each. Store it
   serialized per stage, and deserialize it only when a link needs it.
   Keep it only when fragmentShaderBarycentric is enabled.
 - Each graphics library now holds its own reference on the NIR it uses.
 - Serialize retained NIR without stripping: stripping zeroes the
   locations of function_temp variables, which a later LTO relink needs.
 - On a partial pipeline cache hit, release the shaders that did hit
   before recompiling. tu_compile_shaders treats shaders that are already
   set as final, and linking them could crash in nir_opt_varyings.
 - Move transform feedback outputs that collide with barycentric request
   slots to free VAR slots, instead of failing pipeline creation.
 - Include the mesh and task stages, and mesh_native, in the pipeline
   hash, so that different mesh libraries no longer collide. Cache the
   barycentric producer variant of the mesh stub VS.
 - Fail pipeline creation with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY if
   serialization runs out of memory.

VK-CTS on Adreno 840 (KGSL), one deqp process per group,
TU_EXPERIMENTAL=barycentric,mesh_shader,mesh_native:
  dEQP-VK.fragment_shading_barycentric.pipeline_library.*     5521 / 0 / 1476
    (peak RSS 1.6 GB and OOM before, 371 MB after)
  dEQP-VK.fragment_shading_barycentric.fast_linked_library.*  5521 / 0 / 1476
  dEQP-VK.fragment_shading_barycentric (monolithic)           5521 / 0 / 1476
  dEQP-VK.pipeline.pipeline_library.graphics_library.*        812 / 20 / 4
    (the same 20 failures as before)
  dEQP-VK.transform_feedback.simple.*                         4994 / 0 / 2905
  dEQP-VK.mesh_shader.ext.*                                   26391 / 0 / 547
---
